{"activity_text": "Antifungal, candidacidal, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Bridge", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Host expression: highly expressed in the fat body, followed by the hemolymph, midgut, muscle, and defensive glands. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (69.57%) to Diapausin-1 C: 15%; R=S: 10%. GRAVY: -0.898; M Wt: 4457.971; Mol formula: C176H277N61O60S7; molar extinction coeff: 3355. Activity: active against C. albicans ATCC 10231 and clinical strains (MIC 5.4-7 uM) and T. rubrum (MIC 5.3 uM), but inactive against E.coli ATCC 8739 and S.aureus ATCC 6538. Antibiofilm:fungi: It also inhibited fungal biofilm formation:C. albicans and disrupted fungal biofilm:C. albicans. Antimicrobial robustness: activity is retained at pH 3-5 but reduced at basic pH. Thermostable till 90oC. Activity reduces with the incubation time in human serum for 24 h. In vitro Toxicity: little hemo.lytic till 56.25 uM but almost 50% lysis at 112.5 uM (HC50 >100 uM). No cytotoxicity to mouse RAW 264.7 cells (10 power6 cells/ml) till 225 uM. Es. 5/2023", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37140456", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Microbiol Spectr. 2023 May 4:e0308922. doi: 10.1128/spectrum.03089-22. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03624", "source_id": "AP03624", "source_numeric_id": "03624", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03624", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Blapstin, a Diapause-Specific Peptide-Like Peptide from the Chinese Medicinal Beetle Blaps rhynchopetera, Has Antifungal Function.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
